After ascending a Valkyrie, I wanted to try spell casters next. I had
previously saved Mega the Wizard to the disk, and decided to continue
playing him after the first ascension.

After entering the dungeon, Mega descended quickly to minetown, where
happy things laid in wait. Izchak's had a magic lamp and the temple was
co-aligned. After saccing the monsters in the neighborhood, Mega made
some holy water which was used for blessing the lamp.

The djinn, being very grateful for his release, granted me a nice
shining set of silver dragon scales. Intoxicated with his newfound armor
class, Mega decided to clear the mines in one go. I remember
making a mistake and having a close call, but luckily enough, Mega
survived. His trusty cat Incantation, however, had the (mis)fortune of
stepping into a polymorph trap. He first polymorphed into something I
can't remember, but after stepping there a second time he became a xorn.

With the help of his friend, Mega brutalized the mines' inhabitants,
including the mimics infesting the bottom level. But after he got back
to the town, the unthinkable happened. Incantation started ruthlessly
killing all the inhabitants. I wasn't even able to save Izchak, for
Incantation was able to phase through the walls. :( On the bright side,
he also killed the priest, who happened to drop spellbooks of identify
and polymorph.

Mega spent some time at the altar saccing, and got awarded with
Magicbane and (I think) Ogresmasher. Mega went back to the main branch
and found a scroll shop which (of course) stocked mainly scrolls of
identify. I also managed to get trapped in a shop, somehow owing money
to the shopkeeper (identify?) and having left it all in my stash.

I waited a while and Incantation showed up and pummeled the shopkeeper,
allowing me to filch his goodies. Incantation was gobbling up all the
pick-axes in the dungeon, so I left him and dived for Sokoban. As I had
SDSM, Sokoban was naturally the "oR one. Sokoban, however, fixed my food
problem that I'd brought upon myself with all that identify casting.

Found an altar on dlvl 10 and continued saccing for a while. On dlvl 11
I found a jackpot in the form of bones left by a friend of mine. The
bones contained the bag of holding I was missing, gauntlets of
dexterity, boots of water walking and TWO magic lamps. Used blessed
remove curse for the bones and blessed a lamp. The djinn was again very
grateful, and donated me a nice helm of brilliance.

The helm got polymorph below 100% fail, and I hadn't tried polypiling
before, so I decided to try that one as well. Polyed scrolls and
spellbooks, gaining several useful utility spells. While waiting for
mana to recharge I sacced. As I was baiting monsters on dlvl 11, I found
a throne and decided to try it. The first #sit got me a wish, which was
spent on speed boots. Some more #sitting got a genocide, and arch-liches
were no more.

The wish wasn't all that crucial, though, as polypiling got me a second
set of speed boots soon after. I also polyed up 9 scrolls of monster
creation, 3 scrolls of genocide and 5 scrolls of enchant armor. After
genociding L and h and enchanting up my helm and mail, I continued to
sac and polypile. Cursed the monster creation scrolls and sacced until I
got crowned with the finger.

The quest was easy. Magicbane got off a lucky cancel shot against the
Dark One. With no magic to aid him, he quickly fell to my blows.
Continued descending, and found Ludios using magic mapping. Magic
missile and the finger made it a breeze. The titan on the Medusa level
also got the finger. Mega fell through a trap door soon after, but came
back from below. Medusa got fingered and tinned.

Getting comfortable with his pattern, Mega went to the castle. The
inhabitants were shot with magic missiles and fingers. In the castle
tower a nice surprise awaited in the form of a wand of wishing (0:3).
Mega wasn't feeling particularily greedy, though. He briefly considered
wishing for the mighty Orb of Fate, but as 3 artifacts had already been
generated, he decided to just grab a T-shirt.

Mega had also found a magic marker from the quest and polypiled up a
scroll of charging, so he decided to save the wand for emergencies.
Dried up the marker on scrolls of enchant armor, gold detection and
charging. Mega also performed some alchemical experiments. Having found
no potions of gain energy, Mega was content with the extra healing ones.
They happened to be milky, but luckily only a single ghost emerged
during the quaffing process.

The Valley was uneventful. Mega, still feeling guilty about the Minetown
incident and all that ungodly polymorphing, decided to appease his
conscience and donated all his worldly wealth to the peaceful fellow
tending the altar. Armor class went down to around -39.

Equipped with spells of magic mapping and dig, Gehennom was a lot less
aggravating this time through. Asmodeus was magic missiled to death.
Juiblex had a panic attack and decided to just sit still while Mega
gouged him with Magicbane. He got one turn off which he spent reading a
cursed scroll of create monster, after which the magic-devouring blade
got the better of him. Near the abode of Baalzebub, Mega met a furiously
clucking brood of chickatrices, one of which he put into his bag.
Baalzebub appreciated the gift, and Mega appreciated not having to chase
him across the level. Vlad's was uninteresting except for the nice
amulet Mega found there. He'd found one of those before, but now he had
a spare.

Orcus-town had nothing interesting in it. After purging the town, Mega
was approached by Orcus, who was gloating like only a demon could.
Laughing hellishly, Orcus gulped down a black potion. His plans suffered
a humiliating drawback as the potion turned out to be cursed and Orcus
found himself crashing headfirst through the roof. Mega went after him,
but being the cunning sorcerer he was, decided to burn the name of a
certaing goddess on the upstairs before going up.

This turned out to be a good idea, as Orcus, furious from the
humiliation, summoned his big brother Demogorgon. Mega fled through the
staircase, and quickly burned the sacred word at his feet, as he hadn't
ended up at the stairs. Orcus couldn't take it, and promptly escaped
upstairs, but Demogorgon wasn't quite quick enough. With Demogorgon too
scared to do a thing, Mega mercilessly barraged him with magic missiles
until the mighty demon prince dropped dead. Mega located the cowardly
Orcus upstairs and inflicted just punishment on him, claiming Orcus' dread
wand as his prize.

The strangely vibrating square was found soon after and Mega prepared
for the final descent. Alchemy got HP past the 300 mark. Mega still
thought he'd need a hard hitting physical weapon, as he'd heard obscure
rumors about the Amulet of Yendor draining the magical essence of anyone
who carries it. He gathered up the heaps of weapons he found at the
castle and polymorphed them until he had a stack of eleven daggers.
After rustproofing, enchanting and naming the daggers, Mega started his
final dive. When leaving, he met an Archon at the castle, but it fell
quickly to Mega's stack of daggers. The Archon had Demonbane, which was
stashed.

Upon reaching the wizard's zoo, a furious battle ensued. Noticing Mega
slaughtering his allies, some dastardly demon decided to call for help.
Yeenoghu answered the call. Mega decided to fight fire with (a wand of)
fire and promptly burnt Elbereth on the floor tiles. Yeenoghu was no
match against Mega's new daggers, and being unable to teleport away,
succumbed quickly. The zoo yielded a wraith corpse and a couple of
amulets, one of which was turned into an amulet of life saving before
it shuddered into oblivion.

Mega took the wizard by surprise, waking him up from deep meditation.
Before the wizard could move a finger, Mega moved his own finger,
killing the sorcerer where he stood. After performing the invocation,
Mega found himself in Moloch's sanctum. By now, his diet of wraith
corpses and potions of gain level had elevated him to the status of
Mage. The sanctum's inhabitants couldn't resist Mega's arcane might, and
he seized the amulet without any difficulties at all.

The dreaded mysterious force was found to be quite dormant this time
around. The same could not be said about the Wizard, who resurrected
himself a total of 4 times on the way up, each time eating up a bolt of
black energy.

With no half damage against physical attacks, Mega decided to stop at
the castle to polypile away all his rings in order to obtain a ring of
regeneration, but didn't succeed. Grabbing some K-rations from the
castle's storerooms and all his valuables from his stash, Mega went up
to the dungeon's entrance. After verifying that the Amulet was
authentic, he went to the planes.

Rodney was waiting with his friends the minotaur and the Elvenking. All
three fell quickly to the black bolts of power flying from Mega's
fingers. A previously cursed stack of scrolls of confuse monster
provided confusion and the portal was detected. During the digging, Mega
remembered that he had a ring that sowed discord among his foes and
quickly put it on.

The plane of Air was somewhat scary. The elementals did solid damage,
and with the Amulet draining his mana, Mega was quite uncomfortable. He
almost dried up his wand of polymorph at the elementals. Combined with
conflict, this was enough to make it through safely. The portal on the
plane of Fire was close by and Mega quickly found himself at the plane
of Water. The Air plane had drained his supplies of hit points and
power, so Mega thought he'd need to recuperate a bit. He still had one
of his scrolls of genocide left, and thought it safer to pacify the
level by killing all the sea monsters. After finding the portal and
regenerating, Mega went to the Astral plane.

Due to causing conflict, a hostile angel was sent against Mega. The
angel was no match for Mega's mighty daggers. Detecting monsters, Mega
located Pestilence to his right, Famine to his left and Death in the
center. He had lots of food and the spell of cure sickness at 0%, so he
went for the nearest temple, which was guarded by Pestilence. Mega
managed to slip in the temple without confronting him, but the temple
was found to belong to Anhur. On the way out, he met Pestilence in the
doorway, but the diseased being fell to the mighty staff of Orcus.

Trying his luck with Famine, Mega next headed left. Famine followed the
example set by his comrade and succumbed to Orcus' wand. Mega fought his
way into the temple using magic missiles and his daggers. Famine tried
to follow but the wand again got the better of him. The temple on the
left belonged to Thoth, who received a nice present from Mega.

